## psc/session.pengu — sesión de compilación para F1.
##
## `Session` es dueña de un `SourceFile`, su `DiagnosticBag`, la tabla de
## keywords y las opciones. `Session.open` devuelve siempre una sesión; si el
## archivo no se pudo leer, `ok` es `false` y `error` explica por qué. Así el
## CLI no necesita mover un `Session` fuera de un `result` (el lenguaje no tiene
## move semantics) y no hay que copiar sus listas.
##
## ## Memoria
## `banish session` libera source, diagnostics, keywords y error.

import std.archivum
import std.diagnostic as diag
import std.lingua
import std.sourcemap

import psc.span as pspan
import psc.source as psource
import psc.token as pstoken
import psc.diagnostics as psdiag
import psc.lexer_state as psstate
import psc.lexer as pslexer

## Una sesión de lexación.
##
## ## Memoria
## `banish session` libera todos los campos con heap.
rune Session derive Nexus:
    ## `false` si `open` falló.
    ok as bool
    ## Error de carga cuando `ok == false`.
    error as SourceError
    ## Fuente cargado (vacío si falló).
    source as SourceFile
    ## Diagnósticos acumulados.
    diagnostics as diag.DiagnosticBag
    ## Tabla de keywords.
    keywords as KeywordTable
    ## Opciones de lexación.
    options as LexOptions

## Abre un archivo desde disco.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve una sesión owned; liberar con `banish`.
weave open with path as string, options as LexOptions into Session:
    var m as maybe string is calling archivum.read_bytes with path
    if not m.is_present:
        var empty as SourceFile is calling SourceFile.from_text with path, ""
        var bag as diag.DiagnosticBag is calling diag.DiagnosticBag.new
        var kw as KeywordTable is calling pstoken.keyword_table_new
        var err as SourceError is calling psource.source_error with SourceErrorKind.SrcRead, path, "cannot read source file"
        return with ok is false, error is err, source is empty, diagnostics is bag, keywords is kw, options is options
    var raw as string is m.value
    var f as SourceFile is calling SourceFile.from_text with path, raw
    banish m
    var bag2 as diag.DiagnosticBag is calling diag.DiagnosticBag.new
    calling bag2.add_source with path, (calling f.get_text)
    var kw2 as KeywordTable is calling pstoken.keyword_table_new
    var empty_err as SourceError is calling psource.source_error with SourceErrorKind.SrcRead, "", ""
    calling validate_utf8 with sigil of f, sigil of bag2
    return with ok is true, error is empty_err, source is f, diagnostics is bag2, keywords is kw2, options is options

## Abre una sesión desde texto ya en memoria (LSP/tests).
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve una sesión owned; liberar con `banish`.
weave open_text with path as string, text as string, options as LexOptions into Session:
    var f as SourceFile is calling SourceFile.from_text with path, text
    var bag as diag.DiagnosticBag is calling diag.DiagnosticBag.new
    calling bag.add_source with path, (calling f.get_text)
    var kw as KeywordTable is calling pstoken.keyword_table_new
    var empty_err as SourceError is calling psource.source_error with SourceErrorKind.SrcRead, "", ""
    calling validate_utf8 with sigil of f, sigil of bag
    return with ok is true, error is empty_err, source is f, diagnostics is bag, keywords is kw, options is options

## Registra `E0000` si el fuente no es UTF-8 válido.
##
## ## Memoria
## Añade como máximo un diagnóstico.
weave validate_utf8 with f as ref to psource.SourceFile, bag as ref to diag.DiagnosticBag into void:
    var r as result of void to LinguaError is calling lingua.validate with (calling f.get_text)
    if not r.is_ok:
        var err as LinguaError is r.error
        var off as int is calling lingua_error_offset with err
        var s as pspan.ByteSpan is with start is off, end is off
        var detail as string is "byte {off}"
        defer banish detail
        calling psdiag.emit_issue with bag, f, LexInvalidUtf8, s, detail
    banish r

## Offset de un `LinguaError`.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(1), no asigna.
weave lingua_error_offset with err as LinguaError into int:
    return judge err:
        when InvalidByte with offset -> offset
        when TruncatedSequence with offset -> offset
        when OverlongEncoding with offset -> offset
        when SurrogateCodepoint with offset -> offset
        when CodepointOutOfRange with offset -> offset
        when IndexOutOfRange with index -> index

enchanting Session:
    ## Lexa el fuente de la sesión.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Devuelve un `LexResult` owned; el llamador lo libera.
    weave lex into LexResult:
        return calling pslexer.lex with sigil of self->source, sigil of self->diagnostics, sigil of self->keywords, self->options

    ## `true` si hay errores.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## O(1), no asigna.
    weave has_errors into bool:
        return calling self->diagnostics.has_errors

    ## Renderiza los diagnósticos sin color.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Devuelve un `string` owned; liberar con `banish`.
    weave render_plain into string:
        return calling self->diagnostics.render_plain

    ## Renderiza los diagnósticos con ANSI.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Devuelve un `string` owned; liberar con `banish`.
    weave render_colored into string:
        return calling self->diagnostics.render_colored

    ## Renderiza los diagnósticos forzando ANSI.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Devuelve un `string` owned; liberar con `banish`.
    weave render_forced into string:
        return calling psdiag.render_forced with sigil of self->diagnostics

    ## Renderiza los diagnósticos como JSON LSP.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## Devuelve un `string` owned; liberar con `banish`.
    weave render_json into string:
        return calling self->diagnostics.render_json
